# user.tmux.conf — OPTIONAL agentmux tmux overlay.
#
# Copy to ~/.agentmux/user.tmux.conf and put any tmux settings you want applied to
# agentmux's servers here. It is sourced LAST by the agent, frame, and term sockets
# (via `source-file -q`), so your settings override agentmux's own defaults.
# You do NOT need this file — an absent overlay is a silent no-op. Create it only
# to customize.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#   agentmux runs each project's agent — and, under `amux --frame`, the frame
#   wrapper and its scratch terminal — on its OWN tmux server with its OWN `-f`
#   config. None of them read your ~/.tmux.conf. That isolation is deliberate: a
#   cold per-project agent server that fell through to ~/.tmux.conf would run TPM's
#   synchronous plugin load and stall every launch for seconds. agentmux instead
#   re-sets the sensible defaults itself (escape-time, focus-events, history-limit,
#   mouse, clipboard, …). This overlay is the escape hatch for everything past that
#   fixed list — bring back the pieces of your own config you want, without the
#   plugin-load cost.
#
# FOOTGUN — don't just re-source your whole config
#   You *can* write `source-file ~/.tmux.conf` below, but if that file loads TPM or
#   other plugins you reintroduce exactly the cold-start stall this design removed.
#   Prefer copying the specific bindings/options you care about into this file.
#
# RELOAD & IDEMPOTENCY
#   `amux --reload` re-sources the agent config — and therefore this file — into
#   every live agent server. Prefer idempotent settings (`set -g`, `bind`) over
#   anything that accumulates when sourced twice.
#
# SCOPE NOTE
#   This one file is read by all three sockets. The frame is a purpose-built
#   wrapper with a fixed two-pane layout, so be conservative with lines that rebind
#   its keys or restyle its bar (they can disrupt --frame). The agent pane and the
#   scratch terminal have no such constraint — customize those freely.
#
# ── Examples (uncomment / edit) ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# vi keys in copy mode
# setw -g mode-keys vi

# a bigger scrollback than agentmux's default
# set -g history-limit 100000

# your own status-bar style (agentmux styles the bar per session; this overrides)
# set -g status-style 'bg=colour234,fg=colour252'

# a custom key binding
# bind-key C-r source-file ~/.agentmux/user.tmux.conf \; display "overlay reloaded"

# a custom clipboard pipe (must be here to reach --frame copies — the frame socket
# grabs the drag-select first; see frame.conf)
# bind -T copy-mode-vi MouseDragEnd1Pane send-keys -X copy-pipe-and-cancel "pbcopy"
